    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5632" root="جرى" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرَآءٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِرَآءٌ</span></b>  (S, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرًى</span></b>  (K) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرَايَةٌ</span></b>  (S, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرَائِيَةٌ</span></b>  (IAar, K, TA, [in
the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِرَايَةٌ</span>]) <i>Girlhood;</i> the <i>state of a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَارِيَة</span>.
(S, K.) One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَانَ ذٰلِكَ فِى أَيَّامِ جَرَائِهَا</span> <i>That
was in the days of her girlhood.</i> (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعَلْتُهُ مِنْ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرَائِكَ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَرَى</span>.

